Construction Management Platform

**USER ROLES & PERMISSIONS MATRIX**

*Document 6 of 9 \| Version 1.0 \| Confidential*

March 2026

FOR ENGINEERING & PRODUCT --- CONFIDENTIAL

**Table of Contents**

**1. Overview & Role Definitions**

This document defines every user role on the platform, the default
permissions assigned to each role, and the complete permissions matrix
spanning all functional areas. It is the authoritative reference for
access control implementation.

**1.1 Role Summary**

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Role**         **Scope**        **Who This Is**              **Typical User
                                                                 Count**
  ---------------- ---------------- ---------------------------- ----------------
  **Owner**        Company-wide     The company owner or         1--2 per tenant
                                    principal. Full access to    
                                    everything including billing 
                                    and team management.         

  **Project        Company-wide     Manages one or more projects 2--5 per tenant
  Manager**                         end-to-end. Full project     
                                    access, no billing access.   

  **Estimator**    Company-wide     Prepares bids and estimates. 1--3 per tenant
                                    Read access to projects,     
                                    full access to estimating    
                                    tools.                       

  **Foreman**      Project-scoped   Leads crews on site. Field   3--10 per tenant
                                    data entry, schedule         
                                    visibility, daily reports,   
                                    time management.             

  **Field          Project-scoped   Individual crew member.      5--30 per tenant
  Technician**                      Clock in/out, task           
                                    completion, photo upload,    
                                    daily report viewing.        

  **Accountant**   Company-wide     Manages billing, invoicing,  1--2 per tenant
                                    and financial reporting. No  
                                    field or scheduling access.  

  **Safety         Company-wide     Reviews safety reports,      1 per tenant
  Officer**                         manages inspection records,  
                                    uploads safety               
                                    documentation.               

  **Client**       Portal only      The project owner/client.    1--3 per project
                                    Access only to their         
                                    projects via the client      
                                    portal.                      

  **Sub Portal**   Portal only      Non-tenant subcontractor     Varies
                                    invited by GC. Limited       
                                    portal access --- no         
                                    internal company data.       
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**1.2 Legend**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Symbol**             **Meaning**
  ---------------------- ------------------------------------------------
  **✓ Full Access**      Can perform this action without restriction

  **◑ Limited / Own      Can perform on records they created or are
  Only**                 assigned to; or partial view only

  **✗ No Access**        Cannot view or perform this action --- blocked
                         at API and UI layer

  **--- Not Applicable** Feature does not apply to this role
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

> **Implementation Note:**
>
> Permissions are enforced at two layers: (1) the API service layer
> checks role before processing any request, and (2) the frontend hides
> unavailable actions from the UI. Never rely solely on UI hiding ---
> the API must enforce permissions independently.

