**9. Subcontractor Portal Permissions**

The Sub Portal role is assigned to users representing non-tenant
subcontractors invited to a project by a GC. These users have a
constrained, project-specific view and cannot access any internal
company data of the inviting GC tenant.

**9.1 Sub Portal --- Full Access List**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Feature**        **Sub       **Notes**
                     Portal      
                     Access**    
  ------------------ ----------- ----------------------------------------
  View assigned      Read-only   Sees project name, address, their scope
  project overview               description only. No budget totals.

  View their scope / Read-only   Only tasks assigned to their scope on
  tasks                          this project

  Update their task  Write       Can mark assigned tasks complete
  completion status              

  View schedule for  Read-only   Only phases and milestones relevant to
  their scope                    their scope

  Submit daily field Write       Reports captured under GC project ---
  reports                        visible to GC PM

  Upload progress    Write       Photos stored in GC tenant under GC
  photos                         project --- sub cannot delete

  Create and respond Write       Scoped to their assigned work
  to RFIs                        

  Upload submittals  Write       For their scope --- reviewed by GC PM

  Respond to         Write       Can upload revisions when
  submittal review               revise-and-resubmit
  requests                       

  View applicable    Read-only   Only plans shared by GC on this project
  plan sets                      

  View documents in  Read-only   Only documents the GC has designated as
  their scope                    sub-visible

  Submit invoices to Write       Invoice submitted to GC PM for approval
  GC                             --- sub\'s copy retained

  View invoice       Read-only   Track payment status on their invoices
  approval status                

  Sign lien waivers  Write       Received via DocuSign or platform e-sign

  View lien waivers  Read-only   
  they\'ve signed                

  Receive and send   Write       Thread scoped to sub ↔ GC communication
  project messages               only

  Receive            Read-only   Inspection results, invoice approvals,
  notifications                  task assignments
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**9.2 What the Sub Portal User CANNOT Access**

-   GC company financials, budget, cost data, or margin information

-   Other subcontractors on the project --- cannot see scope, pricing,
    or status of other subs

-   GC\'s client information or client portal

-   GC\'s internal team, employee list, or pay rates

-   Any other projects the GC is running

-   Plan sets or documents not explicitly shared with them

-   Inspection results for other scopes

-   Any data from other tenants on the platform

**10. Role Modification & Custom Permissions**

**10.1 Role Assignment Rules**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Rule**           **Details**
  ------------------ ----------------------------------------------------
  One role per user  Each user has exactly one role. No multi-role
                     support in v1.0.

  Role assigned at   The inviting user selects the role when sending an
  invite             invitation.

  Role change by     Only the Owner role can change another user\'s role.
  Owner only         

  Cannot demote self An Owner cannot change their own role --- prevents
                     lockout.

  Minimum one Owner  Tenant must always have at least one active Owner
                     --- cannot deactivate the last Owner.

  Client role by     Clients receive the Client role automatically when
  portal invite      invited to the portal via the project client portal
                     invite flow.

  Sub Portal role by Sub Portal users receive their role when a GC
  project invite     invites a sub contractor email that is not an
                     existing platform tenant user.
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**10.2 v1.1 Roadmap: Custom Roles**

In v1.1, Business and Enterprise tenants will gain the ability to create
custom roles with granular permission overrides. The v1.0 permission
matrix defines the defaults that custom roles will inherit and deviate
from. Key design decisions for v1.1:

-   Custom roles are tenant-scoped --- no cross-tenant role sharing

-   Custom roles inherit from a base role and can have individual
    permissions toggled on or off

-   Permission changes require Owner approval and are logged in the
    audit trail

-   Custom roles are limited to Business and Enterprise tiers

**10.3 Permission Enforcement Architecture**

Permissions are enforced at multiple layers:

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Layer**    **How Enforced**         **Example**
  ------------ ------------------------ -------------------------------------------------
  JWT Claim    Role is embedded in the  role: \'foreman\' in JWT payload
               JWT token at login ---   
               cannot be modified by    
               client                   

  API          Every API endpoint       POST /projects requires role in
  Middleware   declares its minimum     \[\'owner\',\'project_manager\',\'estimator\'\]
               required role(s).        
               Middleware rejects       
               requests that do not     
               meet the role            
               requirement before any   
               business logic runs.     

  Service      Complex permission       Foreman can only update tasks on projects they
  Layer        checks beyond simple     are assigned to
               role matching happen in  
               the service layer ---    
               e.g. \'can this foreman  
               edit this specific       
               task?\'                  

  Database     Row-level security       Cannot be bypassed by application bugs
  (RLS)        ensures tenant isolation 
               --- a valid JWT for the  
               wrong tenant cannot      
               access that tenant\'s    
               data even if the role    
               check passes             

  Frontend     UI elements are          Foreman does not see \'Edit Budget\' button
               conditionally rendered   
               based on role --- edit   
               buttons, menu items, and 
               forms are hidden for     
               users without            
               permission. This is a UX 
               layer only --- not a     
               security layer.          
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
